  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Control Room",
    "overview": "A calm, high-trust operations desk. Navy chrome frames the work, white bordered panels hold it, and blue appears only where there is an action to take or data to read. Staff use this console to change real people's access, money and journeys, so every surface favours legibility, precision and an obvious next step over expression.\n\nDensity is operational rather than decorative: four-column KPI rows, matrices and tables at desktop width, reflowing to a single column on phones. Depth comes from hairline borders and tonal layering on a pale canvas, not from shadows. Critical actions are deliberately slower: a confirmation with an audit reason, then a fresh password and authenticator check.\n\nAuthority: the API repository's `docs/admin/BRIEF.md` and the private Figma A01–A28 references own layout and business states. Runtime tokens are generated from `src/design/tokens.json` by `scripts/tokens.mjs` into `tokens.ts` and `tokens.css`; components read only those CSS variables. Preserve the supplied logo, Inter typography, navy sidebar, light canvas, bordered white panels, the radius scale and the blue/navy/sky data series.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy sidebar (224px) and white 80px top bar around a mist-grey canvas.",
      "Flat, 2px-bordered white panels with 16px corners; no resting shadows.",
      "One action colour (signal blue); semantic colours only for state.",
      "Every status shows an icon and a label, never colour alone.",
      "English and Swahili at every breakpoint; times shown in EAT."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Action Colour Rule",
        "body": "Signal blue is reserved for interaction and data. Never use it for decoration or as a heading colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Label-With-Colour Rule",
        "body": "State is always carried by an icon plus text; colour only reinforces it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Weight Rule",
        "body": "Inter at 400 and 700 only. A new weight or face needs a design decision, not a component tweak.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Panel Rule",
        "body": "Panels, cards and KPI tiles never cast shadows. Only modal layers do.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do read colours, radii and spacing from the generated CSS variables (`--color-*`, `--radius-*`); edit `src/design/tokens.json`, never hard-coded hex in components.",
      "Do reuse the canonical owners: AppShell/PageHeader for chrome, `src/design/components.tsx` for buttons, panels and KPI cards, `src/design/States.tsx` for loading and recovery, and the shared PasswordInput and VerificationCodeInput for credentials.",
      "Do keep all-time, selected-period and current-snapshot labels distinct, and show loading, denied, expired, stale and retry states with the existing shell conventions.",
      "Do verify at 1440px desktop and 390px mobile, in English and Swahili, by keyboard, and with axe."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add shadows to panels, cards or KPI tiles.",
      "Don't signal state with colour alone, or use slate muted for text on pale fills.",
      "Don't turn an error into a zero value, or show fabricated live results outside the labelled fictional playground.",
      "Don't use Figma AI or redraw the Figma references; deviations from them are logged in the API repository's DECISIONS.md."
    ]
  }
}
